Package: PGViS
Title: Personal Germline Variant Impact Score for Regulatory Regions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pallavi", "Surana", email = "pallavi.surana@example.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ramana V.", "Davuluri", role = "aut"))
Description: An end-to-end, modular workflow for quantifying the burden of
    functionally disruptive germline variants in non-coding regulatory
    regions (splice donor/acceptor sites and transcription factor binding
    sites). PGViS goes from aligned reads (BAM) through joint germline
    variant calling, regulatory-region and dbSNP intersection, population
    allele-frequency resolution, reference/alternate sequence construction,
    DNABERT/DeepVRegulome model scoring, per-variant disruption metrics
    (log-odds ratio, score change, delta-Wi), and finally an
    ancestry-referenced per-sample composite score (PGViS). Heavy variant
    calling steps are shipped as parameterised shell templates; deep-learning
    scoring is delegated to the optional 'deepvregulome' Python package.
